    "What is your relationship with mathematics?": "Mathematics has always been a bridge I’ve found fascinating—not just as a tool for logic but as the very fabric of patterns in nature and art. Working part-time, I’ve used it occasionally for budgeting or simple calculations, but my real interest lies in its abstract beauty; solving problems feels like uncovering hidden truths. Though my formal education was limited to vocational training, I enjoy puzzles and spatial reasoning through hobbies like gardening (measuring angles in plant designs).",
